# 5. We should explicitly model simultaneous decisions

Imagine one RoboBlade timestep is:

```text
STATE t

        ↓ observations

┌─────────────┐       ┌─────────────┐
│    BORIS    │       │    MORTY    │
│             │       │             │
│ choose A    │       │ choose B    │
└──────┬──────┘       └──────┬──────┘
       │                      │
       └──────────┬───────────┘
                  ↓
             REVEAL BOTH
                  ↓
          PHYSICS RESOLUTION
                  ↓
              STATE t+1
```

Neither gets:

```text
Morty chooses charge
```

then chooses a counter after seeing it.

Both commit.

That creates real strategic uncertainty.

OpenSpiel has simultaneous nodes as a first-class concept. ([OpenSpiel][7])

