# 7. Lux AI demonstrates that watching programmed competition can work

Lux AI was explicitly built as both an AI programming competition and a multi-agent RL benchmark. Its first season reports 22,000+ submissions from 1,100+ teams across more than 80 countries. Competitors used approaches ranging from heuristics and search to reinforcement learning. ([Lux AI][10])

One published top-team write-up is especially interesting because they explicitly analyzed both their own matches and high-ranking opponents' matches to discover weaknesses and adapt their approach. ([GitHub][11])

That's precisely your:

```text
battle
↓
report
↓
study rival
↓
change strategy
↓
battle again
```

loop.

Except RoboBladez makes that **part of the fiction as well as the competition.**

