# 13. I would make the strategy game more rigorous than the old design

Here's the version that emerges from this research.

### BEFORE MATCH

Both competitors receive:

```text
public:
    arena
    opponent blade
    mechanical test
    historical matches
    opponent public stats

private:
    own internal memory
    own opponent model
```

Then:

```text
BORIS → policy_B
MORTY → policy_M
```

Both policies are hashed and locked.

No editing.

### MATCH

At timestep `t`:

```text
observation_B(t)
observation_M(t)

        ↓

action_B(t)
action_M(t)

        ↓ simultaneously

physics()

        ↓

state(t+1)
```

### AFTER MATCH

Reveal:

```text
policies
internal predictions
key decision branches
event log
```

Now viewers can see **why** something happened.

